{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Only your flocks and your herds.</b> Earlier, in the plague of locusts, he did not allow them the little ones, but only the men — that is what he said: ״לכו נא הגברים ועבדו את ה'״ — for he said there is no way of the little ones to slaughter sacrifices, and he thought they would not flee once they left the little ones behind. But now, in the plague of darkness, he allowed them also the little ones — that is what he said: ״גם טפכם ילך עמכם״." "<b>But.</b> He wished to hold back in his possession the principal of their wealth and the strength of their riches, which was in the livestock — and this is what he said: ״רק צאנכם ובקרכם יצג״ — and he thought: perhaps if they flee with their little ones, at least the wealth of the livestock will remain to me. And Moses answered him: ״גם אתה תתן בידינו זבחים ועולות״ — that is, you too shall give flocks and herds to make sacrifices and burnt offerings — ״וגם מקננו ילך עמנו״ — it goes without saying that our own livestock shall go with us, and not a hoof shall remain. And what he said, ״זבחים ועולות ועשינו לה' אלהינו״, is as if he said: and we shall make sacrifices and burnt offerings to YHWH our Elohim; ״ואנחנו לא נדע״ — and we do not know with what offerings HaShem will be pleased that we serve Him — perhaps we shall need more than what we have with us. So explained the Ramban, z\"l."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:43.223446909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}